ular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1792681">skiltákn</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1019_36322_570590"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The degree to which a computer, an attached device, a data file, or a program can work with or understand the same commands, formats, or language as another. True compatibility means that any operational differences are invisible to people and programs alike.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="36322">compatibility</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="570590">samhæfi</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10190_122191_571151"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A command button used in a toolbar (or status bar).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="122191">toolbar button</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="571151">tækjastikuhnappur</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10192_233267_1109143"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A business document that is a view of a customer invoice or vendor invoice that documents a payment request but is not an offer or a demand for payment.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="233267">pro forma invoice</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1109143">bráðabirgðareikningur</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10194_228514_1109144"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An indicator of a company's ability to meet its long-term financial obligations, calculated by dividing net worth by total assets.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="228514">solvency ratio</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1109144">eiginfjárhlutfall</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10196_235344_1109145"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The branch of management that plans and controls the holding of inventory. Inventory management does not manage the inventory itself, but rather plans for such things as levels to maintain.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="235344">inventory management</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id=