rNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="571904">flettihönd</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10964_169207_571417"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To reverse changes.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="169207">roll back</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="571417">endurheimta</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10969_233674_1109172"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A group of posting accounts that show the amounts owed to suppliers or creditors for goods, supplies, or services purchased on credit.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="233674">accounts payable</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1109172">lánardrottnar</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10969_314114_1109172"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A group of posting accounts that show the amounts owed to suppliers or creditors for goods, supplies, or services purchased on credit.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="314114">A/P</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1109172">lánardrottnar</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1097_347909_572224"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A user’s private information such as temporary files, history, passwords, web form entries, and cookies that captures Internet surfing and other online activities.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="347909">browsing history</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="572224">vefferill</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10974_39994_570624"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The © character. Normally included at the beginning of a copyright notice.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="39994">copyright symbol</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="570624">höfundarréttartákn</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammatic