uch as a portable music or video player, PDA (personal digital assistant), mobile phone, tablet or warehouse device that works on its own but can also be connected to a computer.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2419401">mobile</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2384392">fartæki</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="12345_763955_2384392"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A piece of handheld equipment such as a portable music or video player, PDA (personal digital assistant), mobile phone, tablet or warehouse device that works on its own but can also be connected to a computer.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="763955">handheld device</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2384392">fartæki</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="12345_81161_2384392"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A piece of handheld equipment such as a portable music or video player, PDA (personal digital assistant), mobile phone, tablet or warehouse device that works on its own but can also be connected to a computer.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="81161">mobile device</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2384392">fartæki</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="12349_26421_1169778"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The process of temporarily storing recently accessed information in a special memory subsystem for quicker access.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="26421">caching</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1169778">vistun í skyndiminni</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="12353_232547_1109281"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Specification that the volume or quantity of a component used in a finished item is proportional to the number of items produced or reported as finished.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="232547">variable consumption</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1109281">breytileg notkun</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="12359_235413_571645"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A modular unit of code that acts as part of a larger system or structure.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="235413">component</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="571645">íhlutur</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1236_42543_1822378"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A file consisting of data in the form of text, numbers, or graphics, as distinct from a program file of commands and instructions.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="42543">data file</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1822378">gagnaskrá</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="12361_233140_1109282"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The categorization of an inventory item based on its value compared to the total inventory on hand.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="233140">ABC code value</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1109282">ABC kóði, virði</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="12362_464497_1956475"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">User's perception about the utility usability and desirability of a product as they integrate it into their lives and their family system. The user experience will be the differentiator that drives adoption and use of hardware software and services.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="464497">user experience</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1956475">upplifun notanda</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="12363_121418_1822420"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In an online forum, such as a newsgroup, a series of messages or articles in which replies to a message are nested directly under it instead of arranged in chronological or alphabetical order.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="121418">threaded discussion</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1822420">þrædd umræða</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="12363_648609_1822420"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In an online forum, such as a newsgroup, a series of messages or articles in which replies to a message are nested directly under it instead of arranged in chronological or alphabeti