 of a strategic goal, objective, plan, initiative, or business process. A KPI is evaluated against a target. An explicit and measurable value taken directly from a data source. Key performance indicators (KPIs) are used to measure performance in a specific area, for example, revenue per customer.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="181005">key performance indicator</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1467941">KPI (afkastavísir)</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="15605_181005_652757"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A predefined measure that is used to track performance of a strategic goal, objective, plan, initiative, or business process. A KPI is evaluated against a target. An explicit and measurable value taken directly from a data source. Key performance indicators (KPIs) are used to measure performance in a specific area, for example, revenue per customer.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="181005">key performance indicator</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652757">árangursmælikvarði</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="15605_181005_652759"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A predefined measure that is used to track performance of a strategic goal,