aticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652814">innkaupagjald</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17104_639828_652776"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A code that represents miscellaneous charges on a transaction, such as invoice fees, freight, and insurance.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="639828">miscellaneous charge code</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652776">gjaldakóði</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17105_639829_652658"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A service for which an employee requires assistance from another person, such as a call center.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="639829">assisted service</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652658">aðstoð við þjónustu</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17106_639830_652663"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An address that points to a bank account.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="639830">bank giro number</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652663">gírónúmer</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17107_639831_652868"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A corporation tax in the Netherlands.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="639831">vennootschapsbelasting</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652868">vennootschapsbelasting</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Other</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17107_639831_652870"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A corporation tax in the Netherlands.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="639831">vennootschapsbelasting</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652870">VpB</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Other</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17107_639832_652868"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A corporation tax in the Netherlands.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="639832">VpB</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652868">vennootschapsbelasting</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Other</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17107_639832_652870"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A corporation tax in the Netherlands.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="639832">VpB</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652870">VpB</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Other</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17108_639833_652839"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A graphical tool that enables fast recognition of entire skill profiles and skill gaps.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="639833">skill gap wheel</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652839">hæfnigraf</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17109_639834_652838"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A method of comparing the actual skill level of an employee with a target level defined for a current job, a career path, or any other job in a company. This analysis helps to identify strengths and weaknesses in an employee's competence profile in relation to a job, and can be used to determine the appropriate competence development activities.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="639834">skill gap analysis</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652838">hæfnigreining</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17111_639881_652697"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The reference point in a compensation range that represents the intended average pay for all employees at that compensation level. For grade structures, control points are typically, but not always, the range midpoint. Broad band structures can use control points but rarely do.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="639881">control point</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652697">stýripunktur</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17112_639885_652723"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The file format for the export of payments.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="639885">export format</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652723">útflutningssnið</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17114_639887_1467925"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The ratio of fixed pay rate to the grade midpoint (or control point) in graded compensation plans. The ratio is used as a measure of how well an employee is paid relative to the grade structure.  The ratio is calculated by dividing the fixed pay rate by the midpoint; for example, an employee with a compa-ratio of less than 1.0 is paid less than the range midpoint. Compensation plans are typically designed so that the average fixed pay rate of all employees at a given grade equals the midpoint of the range.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="639887">compa-ratio</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1467925">uppbótarhlutfall</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17114_639887_652691"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The ratio of fixed pay rate to the grade midpoint (or control point) in graded compensation plans. The ratio is used as a measure of how well an employee is paid relative to the grade structure.  The ratio is calculated by dividing the fixed pay rate by the midpoint; for example, an employee with a compa-ratio of less than 1.0 is paid less than the range midpoint. Compensation plans are typically designed so that the average fixed pay rate of all employees at a given grade equals the midpoint of the range.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="639887">compa-ratio</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652691">samanburðarhlutfall</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17115_639888_652775"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The reference point that is midway between a range minimum and maximum in a graded compensation plan. It represents the intended average pay for all employees at a certain compensation level.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="639888">midpoint</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652775">miðpunktur</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17116_639889_1109514"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Direct or indirect monetary and nonmonentary rewards in exchange for services rendered, or an award for damages sustained by an injury or by the violation of a contract.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="639889">compensation</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1109514">laun</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17116_639889_1587506"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Direct or indirect monetary and nonmonentary rewards in exchange for services rendered, or an award for damages sustained by an injury or by the violation of a contract.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="639889">compensation</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1587506">uppbót</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17117_639890_652787"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A government transaction portal for the Netherlands that promotes and supports electronic communication between businesses and government agencies.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="639890">Overheidstransactiepoort</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652787">OTP</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Other</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17117_639890_652788"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A government transaction portal for the Netherlands that promotes and supports electronic communication between businesses and government agencies.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="639890">Overheidstransactiepoort</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652788">Overheidstransactiepoort</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Other</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17117_639891_652787"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A government transaction portal for the Netherlands that promotes and supports electronic communication between businesses and government agencies.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="639891">OTP</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652787">OTP</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Other</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17117_639891_652788"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A government transaction portal for the Netherlands that promotes and supports electronic communication between businesses and government agencies.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="639891">OTP</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652788">Overheidstransactiepoort</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Other</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17118_639892_652850"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A service that an employee receives without taking action or requesting assistance, such as automatic payroll deposit.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="639892">supplied service</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652850">fengin þjónusta</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17120_639894_652853"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A target award that is defined as a flat award of cash or stock according to compensation level.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="639894">target incentive amount</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652853">hvatningarupphæð markmiða</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17121_639895_652854"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A target award that is defined as a percent of a basis and provided in cash or stock according to compensation level. The basis is usually the annualized fixed pay rate, but can also be a midpoint, control point, or other compensation range reference point.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="639895">target incentive percent</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652854">hvatningarprósenta markmiða</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17122_639896_652858"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The sum of line price variance amounts for a vendor invoice when compared with related purchase order lines.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="639896">total price variance</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652858">frávik heildarverðs</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17123_639897_652861"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The amount of variance between the invoice net unit price and the purchase order net unit price when invoice lines and purchase order lines are compared.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="639897">unit variance amount</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652861">frávik einingaupphæðar</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17124_639898_652866"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Compensation, contingent on discretion, performance, or results, that is awarded to an employee by an organization.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="639898">variable compensation</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652866">breytileg uppbót</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17126_639902_652700"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The process of verifying the credit card holder's identification and credit worthiness before a sales order is processed and fulfilled.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="639902">credit card authorization</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652700">kreditkortaheimild</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17127_639903_1467928"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The process of verifying the credit card holder's identification and credit worthiness before a sales order is processed and fulfilled.  The merchant asks the credit card company to reduce the customer’s credit line by the invoice amount without charging the account. The preauthorization usually expires after a fixed period of time defined by the credit card processor.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="639903">credit card preauthorization</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1467928">bráðabirgðaheimild kreditkorts</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17127_639903_652701"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The process of verifying the credit card holder's identification and credit worthiness before a sales order is processed and fulfilled.  The merchant asks the credit card company to reduce the customer’s credit line by the invoice amount without charging the account. The preauthorization usually expires after a fixed period of time defined by the credit card processor.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="639903">credit card preauthorization</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652701">forheimild kreditkorts</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17128_639904_1467926"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An internal ordered classification that differentiates levels of pay within a compensation structure.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="639904">compensation level</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1467926">launastig</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17128_639904_652692"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An internal ordered classification that differentiates levels of pay within a compensation structure.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="639904">compensation level</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652692">þóknunarstig</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17129_639908_652668"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Dutch Tax Office.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="639908">Belastingdienst</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652668">Belastingdienst</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Other</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17130_639909_652710"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The bank or financial institution that the payment format file is transmitted to for processing.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="639909">depository financial institution</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652710">innlánsstofnun</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17130_639909_652711"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The bank or financial institution that the payment format file is transmitted to for processing.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="639909">depository financial institution</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652711">DFI</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17130_639910_652710"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The bank or financial institution that the payment format file is transmitted to for processing.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="639910">DFI</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652710">innlánsstofnun</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17130_639910_652711"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The bank or financial institution that the payment format file is transmitted to for processing.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="639910">DFI</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652711">DFI</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17131_639911_652732"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Compensation, independent of performance, that is awarded to an employee by an organization.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="639911">fixed compensation</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652732">föst laun</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17132_639912_1467934"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A compensation structure that is used to determine fixed compensation levels (bands, grades, or steps) and the compensation ranges associated with each level. This plan is often used for employees of the same employee type that are within a specific geographical area.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="639912">fixed compensation plan</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1467934">launafyrirkomulag fastra launa</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17132_639912_652733"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A compensation structure that is used to determine fixed compensation levels (bands, grades, or steps) and the compensation ranges associated with each level. This plan is often used for employees of the same employee type that are within a specific geographical area.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="639912">fixed compensation plan</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652733">launaáætlun</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17133_639913_652749"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The company that is associated with an invoice transaction.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="639913">invoice company</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652749">reikningsfyrirtæki</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17134_639914_652756"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Dutch chamber of commerce. All businesses in the Netherlands are required to submit annual financial statements to the chamber of commerce.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="639914">Kamer van Koophandel</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652756">Kamer van Koophandel</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Other</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17134_639914_652761"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Dutch chamber of commerce. All businesses in the Netherlands are required to submit annual financial statements to the chamber of commerce.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="639914">Kamer van Koophandel</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652761">KvK</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Other</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17134_639915_652756"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Dutch chamber of commerce. All businesses in the Netherlands are required to submit annual financial statements to the chamber of commerce.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="639915">KvK</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652756">Kamer van Koophandel</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Other</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17134_639915_652761"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Dutch chamber of commerce. All businesses in the Netherlands are required to submit annual financial statements to the chamber of commerce.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="639915">KvK</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652761">KvK</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Other</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17135_639916_652747"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The file format for the import of payments.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="639916">import format</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652747">innflutningssnið</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17136_639917_652819"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A matching discrepancy between the quantity on a vendor invoice and the matched quantities on the related packing slips.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="639917">quantity match variance</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652819">magnfrávik jöfnunar</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17137_639918_652827"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A one-time award that can be paid out immediately in recognition of special effort, usually in the form of cash, stock, or a gift certificate. Recognition award plans usually involve a nomination and approval process and reward an accomplishment that represents a behavior or value promoted by the company.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="639918">recognition award</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652827">umbun</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17138_639919_652840"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A control that visually represents the complete list of competencies that an employee, a unit, or a team can demonstrate. A skill profile wheel is often used in connection with skill gap analyses, for example to display the difference between an employee's current profile and that of a career path.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="639919">skill profile wheel</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652840">hæfnireglugraf</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17139_639920_1109515"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The ability to proficiently perform certain tasks or duties.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="639920">skill</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1109515">hæfni</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1714_233078_1108828"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A transaction that is recorded in a profit and loss account by an expense transaction.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="233078">accrued cost</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1108828">áfallinn kostnaður</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17153_639951_2600813"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A method of authentication by which the client in a client-server communication proves its identity to the server.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="639951">client authentication</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2600813">auðkenning biðlara</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1716_84183_570939"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A computer hardware component providing access to a network.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="84183">network adapter</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="570939">netkort</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17167_639982_1170906"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To eliminate an entity by removing it from a list, database, or other item, or by uninstalling it.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="639982">remove</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1170906">fjarlægja</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17168_639983_2139447"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To continue a process or service that has been paused.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="639983">resume</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2139447">halda áfram</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17184_640166_1170907"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To set an entity, such as a feature, configuration, or object, back to its defaults.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640166">reset</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1170907">endurstilla</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17188_640172_652693"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A plan that is calculated by summing discrete components and which is usually associated with a span of time. This is often an annual cash bonus plan or other plan that depends on measurable past performance.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640172">composite plan</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652693">samsett áætlun</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17189_640173_652684"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A consolidated customer statement that includes transaction data for all companies in the same organization that a customer does business with.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640173">centralized statement</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652684">miðlægt yfirlit</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17190_640174_652683"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A payment processing system in which one company in an organization manages the incoming and outgoing payments between other companies in the same organization. The other companies still own the invoices. During the settlement process, applicable ""due to"" and ""due from"" transactions are generated.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640174">centralized payment system</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652683">miðlægt greiðslukerfi</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17191_640175_2746801"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An identifier that is given to a customer record to indicate that the customer is the same as a corresponding customer record in another company that shares the same directory ID.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640175">directory ID</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2746801">auðkenni skráasafns</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17191_640175_652715"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An identifier that is given to a customer record to indicate that the customer is the same as a corresponding customer record in another company that shares the same directory ID.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640175">directory ID</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652715">kenni skráasafns</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17192_640176_652717"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A document type definition that contains the definitions for the GdPDU INDEX.XML file.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640176">DTD file</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652717">DTD-skrá</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17193_640177_652726"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The item price that is entered on a purchase order.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640177">extended price</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652726">reiknað verð</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17194_640178_652722"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The anticipated currency amount for a purchase order line, calculated as follows:  Purchase order Net unit price * Invoice quantity.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640178">expected purchase order net amount</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652722">áætluð nettóupphæð innkaupapöntunar</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17195_640179_652725"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A service from BGC that includes a supplementary registration in order to receive reports of all reference numbers on payments made by giro transfer/deposit slip. This service can be extended with controls of the reference number.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640179">extended form registration</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652725">viðbótarskráning</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17196_640180_652678"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A general, nonspecific item that is registered in the system but typically not stocked and often consumed immediately. A category item is used in purchase requisitions when users cannot find a suitable item in a product catalog or by searching all items. A category item must be associated with a product category.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640180">category item</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652678">tegund vöru</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17197_640181_1467923"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A collection of category items that are used only for purchase requisitions.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640181">category catalog</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1467923">tegundalisti</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17197_640181_652677"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A collection of category items that are used only for purchase requisitions.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640181">category catalog</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652677">vörutegundalisti</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17198_640183_652731"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An add-on item to a fixed asset that is considered part of the fixed asset and is not tracked as its own fixed asset, such as an extra battery for a laptop. Typically, an add-on item is maintenance or an improvement and relates to a write-up adjustment.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640183">fixed asset addition</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652731">eignaviðbót</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17199_640184_652736"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A variable compensation plan that rewards employees based on their achievement of a predetermined goal which is usually associated with a program or project that promotes cost-cutting or other productivity improvements.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640184">gain sharing</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652736">hagnaðarhlutdeild</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17200_640185_652742"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A set of default goals that have predefined descriptions to help an organization create specific goals for employees.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640185">goal template</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652742">sniðmát markmiða</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17201_640186_652750"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The actual currency amount that is represented by an invoice line, calculated as follows:  Purchase order quantity * (Unit price/Price unit) - Trade agreement discount + Item miscellaneous charge</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640186">invoice line net amount</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652750">nettóupphæð reikningslínu</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17202_640187_652651"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A practice of matching vendor invoice prices and product quantities to purchase orders and product receipts.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640187">invoice matching</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652651">þríhliða jöfnun lánardrottnareikninga</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17202_640187_652751"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A practice of matching vendor invoice prices and product quantities to purchase orders and product receipts.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640187">invoice matching</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652751">reikningsjöfnun</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17202_640464_652651"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A practice of matching vendor invoice prices and product quantities to purchase orders and product receipts.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640464">accounts payable three-way invoice matching</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652651">þríhliða jöfnun lánardrottnareikninga</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17202_640464_652751"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A practice of matching vendor invoice prices and product quantities to purchase orders and product receipts.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640464">accounts payable three-way invoice matching</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652751">reikningsjöfnun</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17203_640188_652752"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The actual currency amount per unit that is represented by the vendor invoice, calculated as follows: Invoice line net amount / Quantity on the invoice.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640188">invoice net unit price</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652752">nettó einingarverð reiknings</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17204_640189_1467939"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A group of items that controls the allowable price variance percentage for invoice matching.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640189">item price tolerance group</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1467939">vikmarkaflokkur vöruverðs</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17204_640189_652753"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A group of items that controls the allowable price variance percentage for invoice matching.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640189">item price tolerance group</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652753">vikmarkahópur vöruverðs</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17205_640190_652755"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A method of determining compensation by comparing individual jobs to market benchmark data for similar jobs in order to identify a value-relative basis. With this method, a specific pay range is associated with an individual job, but not with a compensation level (grade or band). Job market pricing is a feature of broad-banding compensation structures, but not of grades or steps.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640190">job market pricing</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652755">verðlagning vinnumarkaðar</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17206_640191_652829"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The file format for remittances to a specific bank.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640191">remittance format</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652829">greiðslusnið</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17207_640192_652799"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A compensation plan that is calculated against a base figure taken at a particular point in time. Long-term incentives, such as stock option awards, are often calculated in this way.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640192">point-in-time plan</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652799">tímapunktsáætlun</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17208_640193_652767"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In Australia, a depreciating asset that costs less than $1,000 (after GST credits or adjustments) as of the end of the income year when an organization starts to use it or when it is installed and ready for use for a taxable purpose.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640193">low-cost asset</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652767">kostnaðarlítil eign</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17209_640194_652768"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In Australia, a depreciating asset that is not a low-cost asset but which has an opening net book value less than $1,000 (as of July 1 in the year that it is allocated to the pool), and for which the organization has previously worked out any deduction using the reducing balance depreciation method.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640194">low-value asset</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652768">verðlítil eign</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17210_640195_652769"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In Australia, a fixed-asset depreciation method.  Depreciation is calculated as the sum of low-cost assets (acquisitions) added to the pool in the current fiscal year + second element costs (acquisition adjustments) added in the current fiscal year (depreciated using the low-value pool percentage first-year rate regardless of when they were acquired in the year) + low-value assets added to the pool in the current fiscal year + closing net book value from the previous year (depreciated using the low-value pool percentage rate).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640195">low-value pool depreciation</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652769">afskriftarsafn verðlítilla eigna</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17211_640196_652835"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The capital expenditure on an asset that is incurred after an organization starts to hold it, such as cost of improving the assets in the pool.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640196">second element cost</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652835">viðbótarkostnaður</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17212_640197_1467952"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A factor that enables comparisons and assessments of disparate subjects on a single rating scale.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640197">normalization factor</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1467952">stöðlunarstuðull</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17212_640197_652781"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A factor that enables comparisons and assessments of disparate subjects on a single rating scale.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640197">normalization factor</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652781">jöfnunarþáttur</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17213_640198_1467964"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A group that can be assigned to vendors and that controls the allowable price variance percentage for invoice matching.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640198">vendor price tolerance group</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1467964">vikmarkaflokkur lánardrottnaverðs</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17213_640198_652867"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A group that can be assigned to vendors and that controls the allowable price variance percentage for invoice matching.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640198">vendor price tolerance group</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652867">vikmarkahópur lánardrottnaverðs</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17214_640199_652804"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A matching discrepancy between the invoice net unit price of one or more line items on a vendor invoice and the purchase order net unit price on the related purchase order.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640199">price match variance</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652804">verðfrávik jöfnunar</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17215_640200_652821"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A measure that shows how much of a pay range a given employee has utilized and which is used to determine the potential for additional increases within the range. Range utilization is calculated as follows: (Fixed Pay Rate – Range Minimum) / (Range Maximum – Range Minimum). If fixed pay rate equals the range maximum, then the range utilization equals 100%, pay at midpoint equals 50%, and pay at minimum equals 0%.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640200">range utilization</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652821">nýting launabils</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17216_640201_652828"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A set of activities that are created for a fixed or variable compensation plan. These activities include calculating a guideline increase or award based on the algorithm associated with a specific compensation action, entering a recommended increase or award, presenting the recommendation for approval (if required), and loading the recommendation to the employee.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640201">recommendation work stream</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652828">tillaga vinnutilhögunar</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17217_640202_1467944"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Any type of variance that is detected when a vendor invoice is matched to a purchase order and a packing slip. This may include variances in price, quantity, and miscellaneous charges.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640202">matching discrepancy</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1467944">jöfnunarmisræmi</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17217_640202_652771"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Any type of variance that is detected when a vendor invoice is matched to a purchase order and a packing slip. This may include variances in price, quantity, and miscellaneous charges.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640202">matching discrepancy</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652771">misræmi jöfnunar</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17218_640203_1467943"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Variable compensation that is typically awarded on an annual (or sometimes biannual) basis but which is often paid out over time, with payments beginning at a future point.  This compensation can be determined as a percent of an employee’s annual fixed compensation or it can be related to the number or value of shares in a stock option award.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640203">long-term cash incentive</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1467943">langtíma afkastagreiðsla</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17218_640203_652765"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Variable compensation that is typically awarded on an annual (or sometimes biannual) basis but which is often paid out over time, with payments beginning at a future point.  This compensation can be determined as a percent of an employee’s annual fixed compensation or it can be related to the number or value of shares in a stock option award.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640203">long-term cash incentive</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652765">langtíma greiðsluhvati</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17219_640204_1467961"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Variable compensation that provides the right to purchase company stock at a set price for a set number of years (typically ten). The purchase price (or strike price) is set on the date of the award.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640204">stock option</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1467961">hlutafjárkaupréttur</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17219_640204_652849"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Variable compensation that provides the right to purchase company stock at a set price for a set number of years (typically ten). The purchase price (or strike price) is set on the date of the award.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640204">stock option</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652849">hlutabréfaréttur</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17220_640205_652848"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Variable compensation in the form of company stock that is granted outright. Stock grants are almost always restricted in some manner, and vest over time. For example, a grant of 900 shares may be made available to an employee over three years, with 300 shares transferring to employee ownership at the end of each year. Dividends for the stock, however, are often paid to the employee each year based on the number of shares of the grant retained by the company.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640205">stock grant</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652848">hlutabréfagreiðsla</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17221_640206_652797"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An allowance provided to an employee who is traveling for business. The per diem usually covers lodging, meals and incidental expenses.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640206">per diem</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652797">dagpeningar</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17222_640207_652792"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An employee payment system that is based on measures of goals and reviews. Employees receive increased compensation for their work if they or their team, department, or company reaches certain targets.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640207">pay per performance</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Other</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652792">árangurstengd laun</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Other</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17223_640208_652806"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The difference between an expected price and an actual price.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640208">price variance</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652806">verðfrávik</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17224_640209_652807"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The actual percentage of variance between a purchase order and a vendor invoice, calculated as follows: For positive lines = (Invoice net unit price - Purchase order net unit price)/Purchase order net unit price; for negative lines = (Invoice net unit price - Purchase order net unit price) * -1/Purchase order net unit price</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640209">price variance percentage</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652807">prósenta verðfráviks</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17225_640210_652808"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The allowable difference in prices between purchase order lines and vendor invoice lines that are used for invoice matching.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640210">price variance tolerance</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652808">vikmörk verðfráviks</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17226_640211_652846"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The company from which a centralized statement is printed.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640211">statement company</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652846">fyrirtæki yfirlits</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17227_640212_652795"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The company that is associated with a payment transaction.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640212">payment company</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652795">greiðslufyrirtæki</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17228_640213_1467942"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The currency amount of the price variance between a vendor invoice line and the corresponding purchase order line, calculated as follows:(Invoice net unit price - Purchase order net unit price) * Update invoice quantity</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640213">line price variance amount</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1467942">upphæð línuverðsfráviks</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17228_640213_652764"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The currency amount of the price variance between a vendor invoice line and the corresponding purchase order line, calculated as follows:(Invoice net unit price - Purchase order net unit price) * Update invoice quantity</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640213">line price variance amount</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652764">verðfrávik línuupphæðar</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17229_640214_652815"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The expected currency amount for a purchase order line, calculated as follows:  Purchase order quantity * (Unit price/Price unit) - Trade agreement discount + Purchase miscellaneous charge</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640214">purchase order line net amount</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652815">nettóupphæð innkaupapöntunarlínu</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17230_640215_652816"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The expected currency amount per unit that is represented by the purchase order, calculated as follows: Purchase order line net amount / Quantity on the purchase order</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640215">purchase order net unit price</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652816">nettó einingarverð innkaupapöntunar</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17231_640216_652865"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An individual provision of some form of variable compensation.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640216">variable award</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652865">breytileg umbun</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17232_640217_652779"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An item that is not calculated by Master Planning.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640217">non-direct item</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652779">óbein vara</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17233_640218_652869"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The manner in which-long term variable compensation is distributed to an employee. Long-term incentives are awarded at one time but  distributed at a later time.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640218">vesting schedule</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652869">fleytiáætlun</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17234_640219_652818"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The percentage by which product receipt quantities are allowed to be less than the purchase order quantity.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640219">purchase order underdelivery percentage</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652818">prósenta vanafhendingar innkaupapöntunar</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17235_640220_652817"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The percentage by which product receipt quantities are allowed to exceed the purchase order quantity.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640220">purchase order overdelivery percentage</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="652817">prósenta umframafhendingar innkaupapöntunar</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17236_640221_652803"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A zero-currency transaction sent to a bank to confirm the accuracy of routing and account information.</descrip></descripGr