actions that can be performed based on the content.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="770408">Sticky Notes</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2401262">Minnismiðar</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="21334_770408_2676790"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Microsoft app that creates sticky notes that can be shared between devices, that cloud sync, that are stored on Exchange, and that provide contextual reminders and actions that can be performed based on the content.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="770408">Sticky Notes</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2676790">Microsoft-minnismiðar</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="21335_770428_2411112"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An individual piece of content that resembles a physical sticky note, is displayed across multiple apps and platforms, and that is created using Sticky Notes.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="770428">sticky note</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2411112">minnismiði</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2134_258657_1108847"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A policy that determines which actions are valid for a particular endpoint.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="258657">endpoint action policy</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1108847">aðgerðarregla endastöðvar</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="21348_771258_3045384"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To continue movement, as with the cursor or a search operation, to the beginning or to a new starting point rather than stopping when the end of a series is reached. For example, the screen cursor might wrap around to the first column of the next line rather than stopping when it reaches the last column of the current line. Likewise, a program starting a search or replace operation in the middle of a document might be instructed to wrap around to the beginning rather than stop when it reaches the end of the document.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="771258">wrap around</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3045384">umvefja</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="21353_1177078_1171044"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature that enables presenters in the rich client to broadcast a slide show to remote viewers watching in a Web browser. Throughout the presentation, the remote attendees will see the current slide being shown by the presenter.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1177078">PowerPoint Broadcast Slide Show</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1171044">Senda út skyggnusýningu</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="21353_772635_1171044"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature that enables presenters in the rich client to broadcast a slide show to remote viewers watching in a Web browser. Throughout the presentation, the remote attendees will see the current slide being shown by the presenter.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="772635">Broadcast Slide Show</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1171044">Senda út skyggnusýningu</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="21354_1075942_1171045"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A labeled group of consecutive slides that helps the user navigate and organize presentations.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1075942">presentation section</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1171045">hluti</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="21354_1075942_1171046"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A labeled group of consecutive slides that helps the user navigate and organize presentations.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1075942">presentation section</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1171046">kynningarhluti</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="21354_772636_1171045"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A labeled group of consecutive slides that helps the user navigate and organize presentations.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="772636">section</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1171045">hluti</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="21354_772636_1171046"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A labeled group of consecutive slides that helps the user navigate and organize presentations.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="772636">section</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1171046">kynningarhluti</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="21355_773106_1171047"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature that allows the user to insert the contents of an open window or a screen clipping into the current document without the need to utilize external applications.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="773106">Insert Screen Shot</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1171047">Setja inn skjámynd</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="21358_773112_1171048"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature that makes automatic versions of user documents during each autosave operation and allows the user to revert to previous copies of the document with ease.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="773112">Office Auto-Revisions</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNot