o is followed by a transition to a still image. The combination of video and still image captures the essence of the moment.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2157426">living image</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2346355">lifandi mynd</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="37780_2157427_2181506"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A photo that illustrates motion by blurring together multiple frames of a short video to create the effect of motion in the still image.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2157427">motion focus</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2181506">hreyfifókus</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="37781_2157428_2178976"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The top level view in File Explorer that shows the user's most frequently used and most recently used files and folders or folders pinned by the user for quick access.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2157428">Quick access</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2178976">Flýtiaðgangur</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote