3252_3033536_3034445"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The US federal holiday celebrated on June 19 to commemorate the emancipation of African-American slaves, celebrated on the anniversary of June 19, 1865, the date of the announcement of General Order No. 3 by Union Army general Gordon Granger proclaiming freedom for slaves in Texas, the last state of the Confederacy with institutional slavery.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3033536">Juneteenth</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3034445">19. júní</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="53254_3033546_3034447"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The day on which the US holiday Juneteenth is celebrated if the official holiday itself falls on a weekend.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3033546">Juneteenth (Observed)</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3034447">19. júní (haldinn)</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="53255_3033556_3034440"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The feature in the Authenticator app and Edge that allows users to update their password on a website with one click.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3033556">easy 