 from the system based on auditor or authority requirements.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3126380">audit file</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3126428">endurskoðunarskrá</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="55144_3126381_3126429"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A journal entry made in order to correct an erroneous transaction previously recorded in the general ledger.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3126381">corrective entry</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3126429">leiðréttingarfærsla</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="55145_3126382_3126430"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A document used to track workflow capability when a customer has agreed to make a purchase. You can transfer sales information from a quote, back order, or order to a fulfillment order. After you've tracked the fulfillment order through workflow, the fulfillment order becomes an invoice.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3126382">fulfillment order</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3126430">uppfyllingarpöntun</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="55146_3126383_3126431"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A table in the Business Central database that represents a table, such as an account, in Dataverse. Integration tables include fields that correspond to columns in the Dataverse table.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3126383">integration table</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3126431">samþættingartafla</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="55147_3126384_3126432"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A value of different types assigned to items, which can then be used when searching for those items. Item attributes can be also assigned to item categories, which then apply to the items that use the item categories.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3126384">item attribute</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3126432">vörueigind</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="55148_3126385_3126433"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature that allows administrators to set up the default permissions that new users will get when accessing the system.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3126385">license configuration</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3126433">leyfisskilgreining</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="55149_3126386_3126434"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A VAT that's payable by a purchaser but that isn't deductible from the purchaser's own VAT liability. Companies can usually recover VAT on the purchase of goods and services that are related to their business activities. However, in some situations, a business incurs VAT that isn't deductible. These situations are typically related to the local regulations and can differ among countries/regions.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3126386">non-deductible VAT</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3126434">ófrádráttarbær VSK</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5515_102469_1822406"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A communication mechanism that allows computers to communicate with one another over a network. An RPC consists of a procedure identifier, parameters passed to the procedure, and a value returned to the caller (client computer) after the procedure has executed on the remote system (server computer).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="102469">remote procedure call</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1822406">RPC</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5515_102470_1822406"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A communication mechanism that allows computers to communicate with one another over a network. An RPC consists of a procedure identifier, parameters passed to the procedure, and a value returned to the caller (client computer) after the procedure has executed on the remote system (server computer).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="102470">RPC</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1822406">RPC</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="55150_3126387_3126435"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A mapping between tables in Business Central and Dataverse.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3126387">table mapping</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3126435">töfluvörpun</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="55151_3126498_3126821"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An AI service which can identify information specified by a user in a set of files and pull matching information out of similar files automatically.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3126498">freeform document processing</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3126821">frjáls skjalavinnsla</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="55152_3126499_3126818"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A service that can identify types of files and specific information in them after someone labels the files and provides explanations.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3126499">unstructured document processing</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3126818">óskipulögð skjalavinnsla</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="55153_3126500_3126822"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A category of services that capture, transform, and process data from documents.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term