 365 Supply Chain Management.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3170783">Asset Management</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3171371">Eignastýring</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="56361_3170784_3171372"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An organizational unit that represents the company group or division that is primarily responsible for winning the sale and managing the delivery of work and services to the customer.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3170784">contracting unit</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3171372">samningseining</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="56362_3170785_3171373"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The next-generation, high-performance platform that Dynamics 365 Commerce offers to host the headless commerce engine. It provides the same functionality as the existing CSU, but it's highly optimized and performant because it uses ASP.NET Core and .NET Core.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3170785">CSU Core</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3171373">CSU-kjarni</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="56363_3170786_3171374"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The workspace in finance and operations apps that provides access to important tasks for data management. It also provides information about projects and project execution tasks.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3170786">Data management</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3171374">Gagnastjórnun</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="56364_3170787_3171375"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The set of tools and processes that helps users manage their data effectively.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3170787">Data Management Framework</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3171375">Gagnastjórnunarrammi</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="56365_3170788_3171376"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The omnichannel order fulfillment optimization solution that helps maximize order fulfillment in a supply chain network.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3170788">distributed order management</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3171376">dreifingarstjórnun pöntunar</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="56366_3170789_3171378"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The feature within Microsoft Dynamics 365 that enables users to manage and track their expenses.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3170789">Expense Management</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3171378">Kostnaðarstýring</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="56367_3170790_3171379"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The add-in for Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management which allows companies to model and enforce export regulations in the sales process. User can specify which regulatory governances are in use and classify different types of products and customers. Throughout each step of the sales and fulfillment processes, Export Management checks to make sure the process is compliant.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3170790">Export Management</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3171379">Útflutningsstjórnun</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="56368_3170791_3171380"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The add-in that provides configurable solutions to help users intelligently predict their company's cash flow, predict when they may receive payment for outstanding receivables, and generate a budget proposal that can help speed up their budgeting process.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3170791">Finance insights</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3171380">Fjármálainnsýn</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="56369_3170792_3171381"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The add-in for Dynamics 365 Finance that allows financial and business professionals to create, maintain, deploy, and view financial statements. It moves beyond traditional reporting constraints to help users efficiently design various types of reports.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3170792">financial reporting</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3171381">fjárhagsskýrslugerð</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="56370_3170793_3171382"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A position included in a forecast to create a budget for filled or vacant positions and to estimate payroll elements, such as salary and benefits, for each position.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3170793">forecast position</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3171382">spástaða</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="56371_3170794_3171383"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A total amount for each account in a company's accounting records at any specific point in time, which includes assets, liabilities, equity, revenue, and expenses, and it is used to prepare the company's financial statements.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3170794">general ledger balance</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3171383">fjárhagsstaða</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="56372_3170795_3171384"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The add-in for Microsoft Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management that enables organizations (especially international organizations) to use multiple costing ledgers to do inventory accounting. Therefore, those organizations can comply with multiple accounting standards and internal management accounting at the same time.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3170795">Global Inventory Accounting</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3171384">Altækt birgðabókhald</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="56373_3170796_3171385"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A report that provides details about the inventory physical and financial quantities and amounts.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3170796">inventory value report</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3171385">birgðavirðisskýrsla</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="56374_3170797_3171386"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The feature of Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management designed to provide visibility of goods in transit and calculate the estimated and actual landed cost of shipments.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3170797">Landed Cost</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3171386">heildarkostnaður</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="56375_3170798_3171387"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A service provided by an external provider that stores large volumes of raw data in its native format, handling tasks like data ingestion, cataloging, protection, and optimization, offering businesses cost-effectiveness, scalability, and flexibility for data analysis and machine learning.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3170798">managed data lake</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3171387">stýrð gagnalind</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="56376_3170799_3171388"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A date when a financial instrument expires, i.e. is due to be paid.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3170799">maturity date</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3171388">gjalddagi</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="56377_3170800_3171389"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A policy that lets users establish the sourcing percentages for each vendor.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3170800">multisource policy</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3171389">regla um marga uppruna</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="56378_3170801_3171390"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A legal arrangement between two parties, often financial institutions, that stipulates the terms and conditions for the offsetting of financial obligations. Parties in a netting agreement consolidate their debts into one single payment. This simplifies the process and reduces the risk and cost associated with individual transactions.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3170801">netting agreement</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3171390">greiðslujöfnunarsamningur</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="56379_3170802_3171391"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A limit set on a specific cost, time, or resource that should not be surpassed during the execution or billing of a project.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3170802">not-to-exceed</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3171391">mörk</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="56380_3170803_3171392"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The add-in that enables master planning calculation to occur outside Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management and the related SQL database.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3170803">Planning optimization</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3171392">Fínstilling áætlunargerðar</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="56381_3170804_3171393"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A model that allows to prioritize replenishment orders to ensure that urgent demand is prioritized over less important demand.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3170804">planning priority</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3171393">forgangur í áætlunargerð</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="56382_3170805_3171394"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The feature of Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management that helps B2B companies that are converting to omnichannel pricing by enabling attribute-based pricing rules that use attributes and data from customers, products, and order segments.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3170805">Pricing management</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3171394">Verðstjórnun</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="56383_3170806_3171395"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The feature of Dynamics 365 Project Operations that allows users to create, track, and revise both cost and sales budgets for their projects, and begin tracking actuals against these budgets.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3170806">Project budget management</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3171395">Stjórnun fjárhagsáætlunar verks</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="56384_3170807_3171396"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In financial context, an amount set aside in a company's accounts to cover a future liability or loss that is expected to occur.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3170807">provision</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3171396">reiknuð skuldbinding</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="56385_3170808_3171398"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An expression of a count or sum of an activity that can be used as the basis for allocations or rate calculations. Examples of statistical dimensions include the number of employees, the count of licensed software on each device, power consumption of each machine, or square meters for a cost center.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3170808">statistical dimension</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3171398">tölfræðileg vídd</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="56386_3170809_3171399"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The feature of Dynamics 365 Human Resources that enables efficient entry of employee and employment data. Users can quickly update work history information for past, active, and future employees and contractors.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3170809">Streamlined employee entry</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3171399">Straumlínulöguð starfsmannafærsla</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="56387_3170810_3171400"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The add-in for Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management that enables companies to track products and goods as they move through the value chain, providing valuable insights into the provenance of inputs, supplier sourcing practices, and conversion processes.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3170810">Traceability Service</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3171400">Rekjanleikaþjónusta</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="56388_3170811_3171401"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A promotional discount that is offered by producers to distributors. This temporary reduction of prices for items or services allows the distributor to offer a sale or promotion to customers for a limited time.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3170811">trade allowance</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3171401">afsláttur</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="56389_3170812_3171402"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An entity that stores the relation between two similar business transactions such as cost and related sales actuals or transaction reversals triggered by billing activities such as invoice confirmation or invoice corrections.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3170812">transaction connection</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3171402">færslutenging</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="56390_3170813_3171403"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A solution that helps manage inventory and streamline warehouse and supply chain operations.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3170813">WMS</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3171403">Vöruhúsakerfi</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="56391_3170950_3175786"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A software-based trusted execution environment inside the address space of a host application. More technically, it is a Dynamic Link Library (DLL) loaded by a standard Windows application that secures secrets and sensitive operations in memory.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3170950">virtualization-based security enclave</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3175786">VBS-innskotssvæði</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="56391_3170950_3175787"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A software-based trusted execution environment inside the address space of a host application. More technically, it is a Dynamic Link Library (DLL) loaded by a standard Windows application that secures secrets and sensitive operations in memory.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3170950">virtualization-based security enclave</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3175787">öryggisinnskotssvæði á grunni sýndargervingar</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="56391_3170951_3175786"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A software-based trusted execution environment inside the address space of a host application. More technically, it is a Dynamic Link Library (DLL) loaded by a standard Windows application that secures secrets and sensitive operations in memory.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3170951">VBS enclave</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3175786">VBS-innskotssvæði</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="56391_3170951_3175787"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A software-based trusted execution environment inside the address space of a host application. More technically, it is a Dynamic Link Library (DLL) loaded by a standard Windows application that secures secrets and sensitive operations in memory.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3170951">VBS enclave</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3175787">öryggisinnskotssvæði á grunni sýndargervingar</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="56392_3170952_3174564"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A Windows feature that uses hardware virtualization and the Windows hypervisor to create an isolated virtual environment that becomes the root of trust of the OS that assumes the kernel can be compromised.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3170952">virtualization-based security</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3174564">VBS</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="56392_3170952_3174565"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A Windows feature that uses hardware virtualization and the Windows hypervisor to create an isolated virtual environment that becomes the root of trust of the OS that assumes the kernel can be compromised.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3170952">virtualization-based security</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3174565">öryggi á grunni sýndargervingar</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="56392_3170953_3174564"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A Windows feature that uses hardware virtualization and the Windows hypervisor to create an isolated virtual environment that becomes the root of trust of the OS that assumes the kernel can be compromised.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3170953">VBS</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3174564">VBS</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="56392_3170953_3174565"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A Windows feature that uses hardware virtualization and the Windows hypervisor to create an isolated virtual environment that becomes the root of trust of the OS that assumes the kernel can be compromised.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3170953"