 switched quickly between logical connections on a network.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="15941">asynchronous transfer mode</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="570435">sundurslitinn flutningur</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5865_228520_1108987"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To prohibit the use of a document as a contract.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="228520">void</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1108987">ógilda</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5870_725947_1169747"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature that allows x86-based computers to support more than 4 gigabytes (GB) of physical memory. Up to 64 GB of physical memory can be used as regular 4-kilobyte (KB) pages, and the number of bits that can be used by the kernel to address physical memory can be expanded from 32 to 36.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="725947">physical address expansion</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1169747">viðbót við raunvistfang</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IS