ad key, and the server-write key. Master keys can be exported as simple key BLOBs.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="78635">master key</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="570904">aðallykill</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7870_232418_1822578"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A search folder created in Outlook that provides a view of all email items matching specific search criteria and where the items are still stored in one or more Outlook folder.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="232418">Search Folders</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1822578">Leitarmöppur</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7874_7041_570379"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A string of characters entered by a user to verify his or her identity to a network or to a local computer, device, or client, or to sign in to an account, app, and so on.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="7041">access code</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="570379">aðgangsorð</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="pa