ingular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="931_91234_1956390"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A private telephone network in an organization. Individual telephone numbers or extension numbers are supported, and calls are automatically routed to them. Users can call each other using extensions. They can also place calls to outside numbers.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="91234">PBX</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1956390">PBX</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="931_91235_1956390"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A private telephone network in an organization. Individual telephone numbers or extension numbers are supported, and calls are automatically routed to them. Users can call each other using extensions. They can also place calls to outside numbers.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="91235">Private Branch Exchange</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="is"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1956390">PBX</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ISL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9314_294464_571845"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Personal configurations of a program or operating system.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="294464">pe